{"title":144,"path":145,"stem":146,"icon":104},"SIEM export","\u002Fsecurity\u002Fsiem-export","5.security\u002F7.siem-export",{"title":148,"path":149,"stem":150,"icon":43},"Wazuh and Suricata","\u002Fsecurity\u002Fwazuh-suricata","5.security\u002F8.wazuh-suricata",{"title":152,"icon":153,"path":154,"stem":155,"children":156,"page":49},"Reference","i-lucide-book-marked","\u002Freference","6.reference",[157,162,167,172,177],{"title":158,"path":159,"stem":160,"icon":161},"Agent protocol","\u002Freference\u002Fprotocol","6.reference\u002F1.protocol","i-lucide-arrow-left-right",{"title":163,"path":164,"stem":165,"icon":166},"UI API","\u002Freference\u002Fui-api","6.reference\u002F2.ui-api","i-lucide-braces",{"title":168,"path":169,"stem":170,"icon":171},"Metric storage","\u002Freference\u002Fmetric-storage","6.reference\u002F3.metric-storage","i-lucide-database",{"title":173,"path":174,"stem":175,"icon":176},"Performance","\u002Freference\u002Fperformance","6.reference\u002F4.performance","i-lucide-gauge",{"title":178,"path":179,"stem":180,"icon":181},"Development","\u002Freference\u002Fdevelopment","6.reference\u002F5.development","i-lucide-code",{"id":183,"title":144,"body":184,"description":1132,"extension":1133,"links":1134,"meta":1135,"navigation":1136,"path":145,"seo":1137,"stem":146,"__hash__":1138},"docs_en\u002F5.security\u002F7.siem-export.md",{"type":185,"value":186,"toc":1122},"minimark",[187,200,205,446,460,508,512,549,552,568,572,587,590,608,614,618,643,647,650,756,1106,1118],[188,189,190,194,195,199],"p",{},[191,192,193],"strong",{},"Wolf Settings → SIEM export (syslog)"," (off by default) sends Wolf's security events and its\nsigned journal to a syslog collector. Every minute, the events that match the filters, and every\nsigned journal entry, go out as RFC 5424 syslog (facility ",[196,197,198],"code",{},"local0",") carrying OCSF JSON or CEF.",[201,202,204],"h2",{"id":203},"settings","Settings",[206,207,208,224],"table",{},[209,210,211],"thead",{},[212,213,214,218,221],"tr",{},[215,216,217],"th",{},"Setting",[215,219,220],{},"Values",[215,222,223],{},"Default",[225,226,227,241,253,267,292,305,321,342,361,380,402,434],"tbody",{},[212,228,229,235,238],{},[230,231,232],"td",{},[191,233,234],{},"Export to a SIEM",[230,236,237],{},"on \u002F off",[230,239,240],{},"off",[212,242,243,248,251],{},[230,244,245],{},[191,246,247],{},"Collector host",[230,249,250],{},"a host name or address. With TLS, it must be in the collector's certificate",[230,252],{},[212,254,255,260,262],{},[230,256,257],{},[191,258,259],{},"Port",[230,261],{},[230,263,264],{},[196,265,266],{},"514",[212,268,269,274,288],{},[230,270,271],{},[191,272,273],{},"Transport",[230,275,276,279,280,283,284,287],{},[196,277,278],{},"tcp",", ",[196,281,282],{},"tls"," (RFC 5425), ",[196,285,286],{},"udp"," (RFC 5426)",[230,289,290],{},[196,291,278],{},[212,293,294,299,302],{},[230,295,296],{},[191,297,298],{},"Verify the collector's certificate",[230,300,301],{},"on \u002F off (TLS)",[230,303,304],{},"on",[212,306,307,312,319],{},[230,308,309],{},[191,310,311],{},"Collector CA file",[230,313,314,315,318],{},"a PEM file of a private CA, absolute or relative to the site (",[196,316,317],{},"private\u002Ffiles\u002Fcollector-ca.pem","). Empty: the system CAs",[230,320],{},[212,322,323,328,338],{},[230,324,325],{},[191,326,327],{},"Framing",[230,329,330,333,334,337],{},[196,331,332],{},"octet-counting"," or ",[196,335,336],{},"newline"," (TCP and TLS, RFC 6587)",[230,339,340],{},[196,341,332],{},[212,343,344,349,357],{},[230,345,346],{},[191,347,348],{},"Message header",[230,350,351,333,354],{},[196,352,353],{},"rfc5424",[196,355,356],{},"none",[230,358,359],{},[196,360,353],{},[212,362,363,368,376],{},[230,364,365],{},[191,366,367],{},"Format",[230,369,370,333,373],{},[196,371,372],{},"ocsf",[196,374,375],{},"cef",[230,377,378],{},[196,379,372],{},[212,381,382,387,398],{},[230,383,384],{},[191,385,386],{},"Minimum severity",[230,388,389,279,392,279,395],{},[196,390,391],{},"info",[196,393,394],{},"warning",[196,396,397],{},"critical",[230,399,400],{},[196,401,394],{},[212,403,404,409,430],{},[230,405,406],{},[191,407,408],{},"Event types",[230,410,411,412,279,415,279,418,279,421,279,424,279,427],{},"comma-separated: ",[196,413,414],{},"security",[196,416,417],{},"error",[196,419,420],{},"cron_failure",[196,422,423],{},"worker_failure",[196,425,426],{},"host_metric_alert",[196,428,429],{},"deployment",[230,431,432],{},[196,433,414],{},[212,435,436,441,444],{},[230,437,438],{},[191,439,440],{},"Send the journal",[230,442,443],{},"also send every signed journal entry (seq, digest, mac)",[230,445,304],{},[188,447,448,449,452,453,456,457,459],{},"To check a collector, a Wolf Manager can POST to ",[196,450,451],{},"dodock_wolf.api.siem.send_test",". It sends one\n",[196,454,455],{},"wolf_test"," message with the current settings, even while ",[191,458,234],{}," is off:",[461,462,467],"pre",{"className":463,"code":464,"language":465,"meta":466,"style":466},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","curl -X POST -H \"Authorization: token \u003Capi_key>:\u003Capi_secret>\" \\\n  https:\u002F\u002Fwolf.example.com\u002Fapi\u002Fmethod\u002Fdodock_wolf.api.siem.send_test\n","bash","",[196,468,469,502],{"__ignoreMap":466},[470,471,474,478,482,485,488,492,495,498],"span",{"class":472,"line":473},"line",1,[470,475,477],{"class":476},"sBMFI","curl",[470,479,481],{"class":480},"sfazB"," -X",[470,483,484],{"class":480}," POST",[470,486,487],{"class":480}," -H",[470,489,491],{"class":490},"sMK4o"," \"",[470,493,494],{"class":480},"Authorization: token \u003Capi_key>:\u003Capi_secret>",[470,496,497],{"class":490},"\"",[470,499,501],{"class":500},"sTEyZ"," \\\n",[470,503,505],{"class":472,"line":504},2,[470,506,507],{"class":480},"  https:\u002F\u002Fwolf.example.com\u002Fapi\u002Fmethod\u002Fdodock_wolf.api.siem.send_test\n",[509,510,367],"h3",{"id":511},"format",[513,514,515,530],"ul",{},[516,517,518,521,522,525,526,529],"li",{},[191,519,520],{},"OCSF",": JSON, Detection Finding (class 2004). ATT&CK techniques in ",[196,523,524],{},"finding_info.attacks",";\nWolf's site, bench and payload under ",[196,527,528],{},"unmapped",". The mapping is Wolf's reading of the schema,\nnot a certified profile.",[516,531,532,535,536,279,539,544,545,548],{},[191,533,534],{},"CEF",": ATT&CK in ",[196,537,538],{},"cs4",[540,541,543],"a",{"href":542},"\u002Fsecurity\u002Fjournal#ip-reputation-lists","IP reputation"," lists in ",[196,546,547],{},"cs5",".",[509,550,348],{"id":551},"message-header",[513,553,554,563],{},[516,555,556,558,559,562],{},[196,557,353],{},": a syslog header before each message: priority, timestamp, the site as host name,\n",[196,560,561],{},"dodock-wolf"," as application, the event category as MSGID.",[516,564,565,567],{},[196,566,356],{},": the bare JSON or CEF, for collectors that decode the message themselves, such as\nWazuh's JSON decoder and Graylog's CEF input.",[509,569,571],{"id":570},"transport-and-framing","Transport and framing",[513,573,574,577,582],{},[516,575,576],{},"Prefer TCP or TLS. UDP sends one datagram per message, cut at 8 KB. Wolf cannot tell whether\nthe collector got anything, so the cursor moves anyway.",[516,578,579,581],{},[196,580,332],{}," precedes each message with its length. rsyslog, syslog-ng and Graylog's Syslog\ninput read it.",[516,583,584,586],{},[196,585,336],{}," sends one message per line; a line break inside a message becomes a space. Wazuh and\nGraylog's CEF input need it.",[509,588,589],{"id":282},"TLS",[513,591,592,597],{},[516,593,594,595,548],{},"The collector's certificate is checked against the system CAs, or ",[191,596,311],{},[516,598,599,600,603,604,607],{},"Python 3.13 and later verify strictly: the CA needs ",[196,601,602],{},"basicConstraints=CA:TRUE"," and\n",[196,605,606],{},"keyUsage=keyCertSign",", and the server certificate needs an Authority Key Identifier.",[609,610,611],"caution",{},[188,612,613],{},"Turning certificate verification off works, but anyone on the path can then read the export.",[201,615,617],{"id":616},"delivery","Delivery",[513,619,620,623,626,629,636],{},[516,621,622],{},"A cursor moves only after a batch is sent. A collector that is down delays the export; nothing\nis skipped.",[516,624,625],{},"A failure mid-batch can send a message twice: delivery is at least once.",[516,627,628],{},"Events younger than 2 minutes wait for the next run, so a transaction that commits a little\nafter it inserted is not skipped.",[516,630,631,632,635],{},"Payloads go out as they are stored (already ",[540,633,634],{"href":71},"scrubbed"," by the agent), cut at\n4 KB.",[516,637,638,639,548],{},"Journal entries give the SIEM an external copy of the chain: an anchor Wolf cannot rewrite. See\n",[540,640,642],{"href":641},"\u002Fsecurity\u002Fjournal#tamper-evident-journal","Tamper-evident journal",[201,644,646],{"id":645},"collectors","Collectors",[188,648,649],{},"Each recipe was tried against the real collector (November 2026).",[206,651,652,670],{},[209,653,654],{},[212,655,656,659,661,663,665,667],{},[215,657,658],{},"Collector",[215,660,367],{},[215,662,348],{},[215,664,273],{},[215,666,327],{},[215,668,669],{},"What you get",[225,671,672,695,716,736],{},[212,673,674,677,680,684,687,692],{},[230,675,676],{},"rsyslog 8.2404",[230,678,679],{},"OCSF or CEF",[230,681,682],{},[196,683,353],{},[230,685,686],{},"UDP, TCP or TLS",[230,688,689,691],{},[196,690,332],{}," (TCP\u002FTLS)",[230,693,694],{},"messages written as sent; MSGID is the event category",[212,696,697,700,702,706,709,713],{},[230,698,699],{},"Wazuh 4.9.2 manager",[230,701,520],{},[230,703,704],{},[196,705,356],{},[230,707,708],{},"TCP",[230,710,711],{},[196,712,336],{},[230,714,715],{},"one Wazuh alert per finding, level by severity",[212,717,718,721,723,727,729,733],{},[230,719,720],{},"Graylog 6.1, CEF input",[230,722,534],{},[230,724,725],{},[196,726,356],{},[230,728,708],{},[230,730,731],{},[196,732,336],{},[230,734,735],{},"every field extracted (source address, ATT&CK, site, severity)",[212,737,738,741,743,747,749,753],{},[230,739,740],{},"Graylog 6.1, Syslog input",[230,742,679],{},[230,744,745],{},[196,746,353],{},[230,748,686],{},[230,750,751],{},[196,752,332],{},[230,754,755],{},"messages stored, JSON not split into fields",[757,758,759,780,1016,1100],"tabs",{},[760,761,763,772],"tabs-item",{"label":762},"rsyslog",[461,764,770],{"className":765,"code":767,"filename":768,"language":769,"meta":466},[766],"language-text","module(load=\"imptcp\")                     # TCP, octet-counted or newline\ninput(type=\"imptcp\" port=\"514\")\nmodule(load=\"imtcp\" StreamDriver.Name=\"gtls\" StreamDriver.Mode=\"1\" StreamDriver.AuthMode=\"anon\")\ninput(type=\"imtcp\" port=\"6514\")           # TLS (global DefaultNetstreamDriver* point at the cert)\nmodule(load=\"imudp\")\ninput(type=\"imudp\" port=\"514\")\n","rsyslog.conf","text",[196,771,767],{"__ignoreMap":466},[188,773,774,775,279,777,779],{},"The default Wolf settings work: ",[196,776,353],{},[196,778,332],{},", OCSF or CEF.",[760,781,783,926,983,999,1002],{"label":782},"Wazuh",[784,785,786,898,912],"ol",{},[516,787,788,789,792,793],{},"On the manager, add a syslog input to ",[196,790,791],{},"\u002Fvar\u002Fossec\u002Fetc\u002Fossec.conf",":",[461,794,799],{"className":795,"code":796,"filename":797,"language":798,"meta":466,"style":466},"language-xml shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","\u003Cremote>\n  \u003Cconnection>syslog\u003C\u002Fconnection>\n  \u003Cport>514\u003C\u002Fport>\n  \u003Cprotocol>tcp\u003C\u002Fprotocol>\n  \u003Callowed-ips>WOLF_SITE_ADDRESS\u002F32\u003C\u002Fallowed-ips>\n\u003C\u002Fremote>\n","ossec.conf","xml",[196,800,801,813,834,852,870,889],{"__ignoreMap":466},[470,802,803,806,810],{"class":472,"line":473},[470,804,805],{"class":490},"\u003C",[470,807,809],{"class":808},"swJcz","remote",[470,811,812],{"class":490},">\n",[470,814,815,818,821,824,827,830,832],{"class":472,"line":504},[470,816,817],{"class":490},"  \u003C",[470,819,820],{"class":808},"connection",[470,822,823],{"class":490},">",[470,825,826],{"class":500},"syslog",[470,828,829],{"class":490},"\u003C\u002F",[470,831,820],{"class":808},[470,833,812],{"class":490},[470,835,837,839,842,844,846,848,850],{"class":472,"line":836},3,[470,838,817],{"class":490},[470,840,841],{"class":808},"port",[470,843,823],{"class":490},[470,845,266],{"class":500},[470,847,829],{"class":490},[470,849,841],{"class":808},[470,851,812],{"class":490},[470,853,855,857,860,862,864,866,868],{"class":472,"line":854},4,[470,856,817],{"class":490},[470,858,859],{"class":808},"protocol",[470,861,823],{"class":490},[470,863,278],{"class":500},[470,865,829],{"class":490},[470,867,859],{"class":808},[470,869,812],{"class":490},[470,871,873,875,878,880,883,885,887],{"class":472,"line":872},5,[470,874,817],{"class":490},[470,876,877],{"class":808},"allowed-ips",[470,879,823],{"class":490},[470,881,882],{"class":500},"WOLF_SITE_ADDRESS\u002F32",[470,884,829],{"class":490},[470,886,877],{"class":808},[470,888,812],{"class":490},[470,890,892,894,896],{"class":472,"line":891},6,[470,893,829],{"class":490},[470,895,809],{"class":808},[470,897,812],{"class":490},[516,899,900,901,907,908,911],{},"Copy the ",[540,902,906],{"href":903,"rel":904},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fbthuner\u002Fdodock-wolf\u002Fblob\u002Fmain\u002Fdocs\u002Fsiem\u002Fwazuh_dodock_wolf_rules.xml",[905],"nofollow","rules file","\nto ",[196,909,910],{},"\u002Fvar\u002Fossec\u002Fetc\u002Frules\u002F"," and restart the manager. It needs Wazuh 4.6 or later.",[516,913,914,915,917,918,920,921,923,924,548],{},"Set Wolf to: format ",[196,916,372],{},", message header ",[196,919,356],{},", transport ",[196,922,278],{},", framing ",[196,925,336],{},[206,927,928,941],{},[209,929,930],{},[212,931,932,935,938],{},[215,933,934],{},"Wolf finding",[215,936,937],{},"Wazuh rule",[215,939,940],{},"Level",[225,942,943,953,963,973],{},[212,944,945,947,950],{},[230,946,391],{},[230,948,949],{},"100901",[230,951,952],{},"3",[212,954,955,957,960],{},[230,956,394],{},[230,958,959],{},"100902",[230,961,962],{},"7",[212,964,965,967,970],{},[230,966,397],{},[230,968,969],{},"100903",[230,971,972],{},"12",[212,974,975,978,981],{},[230,976,977],{},"journal entry",[230,979,980],{},"100910",[230,982,952],{},[188,984,985,986,279,989,992,993,279,995,998],{},"The OCSF fields become Wazuh fields: ",[196,987,988],{},"src_endpoint.ip",[196,990,991],{},"finding_info.title",",\n",[196,994,524],{},[196,996,997],{},"unmapped.site",", and so on.",[188,1000,1001],{},"Does not work with Wazuh:",[513,1003,1004,1007,1010,1013],{},[516,1005,1006],{},"the RFC 5424 header: Wazuh does not parse it, so only a generic rule fires;",[516,1008,1009],{},"CEF: Wazuh has no decoder for it;",[516,1011,1012],{},"octet-counted frames: they are dropped;",[516,1014,1015],{},"TLS: Wazuh's syslog input has none. Put a local relay (rsyslog, stunnel) in front when the\nnetwork between Wolf and Wazuh is not trusted.",[760,1017,1019,1038,1085],{"label":1018},"Graylog",[188,1020,1021,1024,1025,1028,1029,1031,1032,920,1034,923,1036,548],{},[191,1022,1023],{},"To get fields",": create a ",[191,1026,1027],{},"CEF TCP"," input, then set Wolf to: format ",[196,1030,375],{},", message header\n",[196,1033,356],{},[196,1035,278],{},[196,1037,336],{},[513,1039,1040,1070,1076],{},[516,1041,1042,1043,279,1046,1049,1050,279,1053,992,1056,279,1059,1062,1063,1066,1067,548],{},"The input extracts ",[196,1044,1045],{},"sourceAddress",[196,1047,1048],{},"deviceHostName"," (the site), ",[196,1051,1052],{},"mitre_attack",[196,1054,1055],{},"site",[196,1057,1058],{},"severity",[196,1060,1061],{},"event_class_id"," (the category) and the journal's ",[196,1064,1065],{},"digest"," \u002F ",[196,1068,1069],{},"mac",[516,1071,1072,1075],{},[196,1073,1074],{},"source"," is the address of the Wolf site.",[516,1077,1078,1079,1081,1082,548],{},"The RFC 5424 header confuses this input: ",[196,1080,1074],{}," becomes ",[196,1083,1084],{},"-",[188,1086,1087,1090,1091,992,1093,1095,1096,1099],{},[191,1088,1089],{},"To store only",": the Syslog TCP, UDP or TLS inputs accept the default settings (",[196,1092,353],{},[196,1094,332],{},"). Graylog keeps MSGID and the structured-data dash at the start of ",[196,1097,1098],{},"message","\nand does not split the JSON. Add a JSON extractor or a pipeline rule if you take this road.",[760,1101,1103],{"label":1102},"UniSOC and others",[188,1104,1105],{},"UniSOC has not been tried, for lack of an instance. Any collector that takes syslog with\nRFC 5424, CEF or JSON lines should work with one of the combinations above.",[1107,1108,1109],"note",{},[188,1110,1111,1112,1115,1116,548],{},"When Wolf exports to a Wazuh manager that the Wolf Agent also reads, Wazuh's alerts on Wolf's own\nexport (group ",[196,1113,1114],{},"dodock_wolf",") are always left out, so nothing loops back. See\n",[540,1117,148],{"href":149},[1119,1120,1121],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sBMFI, html code.shiki .sBMFI{--shiki-light:#E2931D;--shiki-default:#FFCB6B;--shiki-dark:#FFCB6B}html pre.shiki code .sfazB, html code.shiki .sfazB{--shiki-light:#91B859;--shiki-default:#C3E88D;--shiki-dark:#C3E88D}html pre.shiki code .sMK4o, html code.shiki .sMK4o{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF}html pre.shiki code .sTEyZ, html code.shiki .sTEyZ{--shiki-light:#90A4AE;--shiki-default:#EEFFFF;--shiki-dark:#BABED8}html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html .default .shiki span {